fontforge-wasm patch 9. Reason: two defects in GPOS device tables (hinting deltas per ppem), found with patch 8.
(1) OpenType counts a PairPosFormat1's value-record device offsets "from beginning of the immediate parent table ...
PairSet table within a PairPosFormat1 lookup subtable", as fontTools and HarfBuzz read them; gposKernSubTable read
them from the subtable, and dumpGPOSpairpos wrote them from the subtable, with each glyph's tables before its PairSet.
A conforming font's tables were read at the wrong place (dropped with "Bad device table", or taken from unrelated
bytes), and every table FontForge wrote was misread by everyone else. Now the reader counts from the PairSet, and the
writer puts a PairSet's tables after its records and counts from the PairSet. (2) dumpGPOSsimplepos format 2 wrote the
first glyph's device tables for every glyph while each glyph's offsets counted its own, and followed a NULL pointer
when the first glyph had none (native: SEGV; wasm: tables missing, offsets past the end). It now writes each glyph's
own tables. The class-pair writer and reader already count from the subtable, as OpenType says for format 2.
Owner's decision of 2026-11-18; fixture generated/layout/slick-gpos-devices.ttf (fontconverter-web 7d28e31).

